    "created_at": "2016-12-09T01:31:12Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-12-09T01:31:12Z",
    "body": "Service worker checks a new service worker version by comparing the existing service worker's script and the newly fetched script. I found we haven't considered module script case for that and changed related text: https://github.com/w3c/ServiceWorker/pull/1020#discussion-diff-91540889R2530. In that change, I tried to access the _module record_'s [[ECMAScriptCode]] for the equality check. Would that be a right way to compare two module scripts btw?",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
